# Spatial extension of the original native Wilson source

The source rule in this proof extends the original native Wilson–Maxwell
construction to open cubical boxes. It retains the native constituent
Hamiltonian, the selected source excitation m, `g=1/64`, `a=1/m`, the
complete four-constituent occupation code per macrovertex, all old/dual/
port and spin references, the global code guard, and the positive
macrocell completion coefficient c(g). Box size and total photon cap
are declared finite parameters. The fixed-cube ground and record
receipts are unchanged.

The accepted state is a nonstationary free Wilson/code vacuum prepared
by complete code-admission records. No interacting-ground theorem is
transferred to a larger box. The exact spectral/code projectors and
programmable finite-matrix controls are declared apparatus services,
as they are in the source's guarded matrix-unit construction. Their
efficient implementation by the passive repair law is not proved.

## Exact open-box geometry and the finite carrier

For n cells per coordinate axis, put `N=n+1`, `V=N^3`,
`E=3nN^2`, and `d=E-V+1`. The source's actual cochain constructor gives
the incidence D and oriented face boundary C, with `C D=0`. There
are no harmonic one-forms on this contractible box. The transverse
photon space has dimension d; the executed cases n=1,2,3 give d=5,28,81.

The one-form Hodge operator is
`L_1=D D^T+C^T C`. In an axis-grouped edge ordering it is the direct
sum of three tensor-product Laplacians. Along the edge's own axis the
one-dimensional matrix has diagonal 2 and adjacent entries -1, on n
coordinates. Along either other axis it is the path-graph Laplacian
on N coordinates, with endpoint diagonal 1 and interior diagonal 2.
The producer checks this identity against the literal source cochains.
The elementary sine/cosine eigenfunctions have

`lambda_k=4 sin^2(pi k/(2N)), k=0,...,n`.

A multi-index with r nonzero components admits r one-form components.
One is longitudinal and r-1 are transverse. Thus

`nu_min=2sqrt(2) sin(pi/(2N))>=2sqrt(2)/N`,
`nu_max<sqrt(12)`.

The physical frequencies are `nu/a=m nu`. In particular the free
transverse photon gap tends to zero as the volume grows. A uniform
positive full-ground gap cannot be imported from the eight-vertex
proof. The fixed c(g) does not supply a larger-volume interacting-ground
selection theorem; it vanishes on the whole code and cannot change
the free photon infrared gap.

Each vertex has four complete native constituents, with the same
sixteen-state code and all complementary native states retained.
The physical density is the same oriented global-frame expression
`rho_x=U_FW Q_native,x U_FW^dagger`. The full density spectrum is in
`[-4,4]`. The outer integer-Gauss registers are `9^(V-1)` longitudinal
labels and one `(8V+1)`-state compensator, `R=-sum rho`, with cost
`4|R|`. The normalized constraints do not depend on g. With
`G=(D^T D)^+` and `rho_ref=(I-e_root ones^T)rho`,

`P_L=g D G rho_ref`, `H_C=m g^2 rho_ref^T G rho_ref/2`.

The same physical isometry Y coherently attaches these labels. Its
outer-constraint-orthogonal extension remains zero for the source
Hamiltonian and identity for physical unitaries. Native Gauss-violating
states remain in the native complement and have zero probability under
the physical preparation. No continuous carrier is in a finite member.

Choose a total occupation cap K on the d transverse modes. Its exact
dimension is `binom(K+d,d)`. The literal finite coordinates are
compressed linear oscillator coordinates, and the links are their
finite exponentials. The positive boundary completion gives exactly

`H_ph=m[sum_j nu_j/2+dGamma(nu)]`.

All zero points remain in the raw clock. The source Hamiltonian is
the same sum of native constituents, positive free-code kinetic
correction, completed field energy, reference and Coulomb energies,
globally guarded Peierls correction, and
`m c(g) sum_x(I-P_x)`. Every P_x reduces every term, by the same
spectral/charge and Gauss-intertwiner proof as on the cube.

The open Wilson one-body gap needed to define the code kinetic
correction is uniform. Write `h=A+beta M`, with A self-adjoint,
`{A,beta}=0`, and `M=m+L_vertex/(2a)>=m`. Then
`Re<beta psi,h psi>=<psi,M psi>>=m||psi||^2`, so `||h psi||>=m||psi||`.
Along the continuous interpolation from m beta to h there is no zero
crossing; the positive and negative ranks are each 2V. The added
quasiparticle energies `|E|-m` are therefore nonnegative. This is a
free code construction, not an interacting many-body gap claim.

## Complete code-bank preparation

Let p0 be the inherited lower bound for the unfiltered native trial's
ground overlap. It is a source number, not a measured calibration.
The added R_loc registers start in their shared vacuum. On a macrocell,
the exact sixteen-occupation projector then has the support identity

`P_x |trial^4,R_loc=vac> = |g^4,ports=vac> tensor chi`,

with squared norm at least `p_cell=p0^4`. The vector chi contains every
retained original preparation reference. Every other code occupation
has a nonvacuum port, so none is present in this intersection. This
identity does not assume that the unfiltered native trial equals g.

Prepare R independent full-box trials and measure every P_x in every
bank with a binary pointer. All these projections commute. Y commutes
or intertwines each P_x, so their probabilities are the same as before
the physical Gauss embedding and factor across cells and banks.
All `V R` binary outcomes, including failures, are retained.

For each vertex choose the first successful bank. A flag-controlled
swap of that entire logical macrocell into the active bank assembles
the product `g^(4V)` whenever every cell has a success. The physical
swap is `Y_total S_swap Y_total^dagger`, with identity on the outer
constraint complement. It updates the charge-reference labels
coherently and preserves all native Gauss constraints. The original
spin references may be swapped with their macrocell; in either
convention the projected source ground factor is pure and separates
from every retained environment. All unused banks and flags remain.

The active accepted state is exactly the source's free Wilson vacuum
in its full occupation code, with photon vacuum and the actual Gauss
reference. It is not the coupled ground. A conditional global success
bit copies the logical AND of the per-cell admission records. On any
failure, all subsequent observer slots execute retained no-op records.

With `f=1-p0^4`, the original-attempt failure probability is at most
`V f^R`. For example choose

`R=min{r>=1:V f^r<=2^-40/(V+1)^2}`.

The executed examples n=1,2,3,7 use three full-box banks; n=15,31 use
four. The resource growth is logarithmic in V in bank count. There is
no repeated-until-success loop or discarded unsuccessful trial.

The code projector is an exact existing source matrix service, not an
implemented finite phase-estimation approximation. Its controlled
binary measurement is bounded and complete. An additional certified
implementation error would enter the complete-isometry comparison
before success conditioning. This premise cannot be replaced by a
claim that a ground projector was obtained from a short native clock.

Three duration-one driven slots implement trial preparation, all code
flags, and routing. Each uses a specified finite Hermitian logarithm
and the actual total background Hamiltonian cancellation. A subsequent
bundled local detector uses its own duration-one slot and final common
source evolution. Thus equal-time local histories have elapsed source
time four on every success and failure branch. An autonomous wait T
adds T on every bank; it is included explicitly in the cutoff theorem.
These are global programmable preparation controls, not a local
autonomous preparation dynamics.

## Uniform physical propagation and finite photon budgets

On the reducing code the same gauge-parent/direct-integral argument
as in the fixed-cube locality proof applies at every finite n. The
longitudinal point fiber is a mathematical comparison, not a
normalizable state in an added gauge register. Total-charge reference
costs commute with the gauge-invariant observable net and remain in
the physical clock.

For a bounded gauge-invariant unitary intervention, the actual
electric/magnetic/current commutators are dominated by the same
nonnegative matrix on `(q_e,p_e,z_x)`:

`q'<=p`,
`p'<=(|C^T C|+4g^2 I)q+4g S z`,
`z'<=A_vertices z+2g S^T q`.

An edge belongs to at most four faces and each face has four edges.
Consequently `|| |C^T C| ||_infinity<=16`, and vertex degree is at
most six. A uniform row bound is

`kappa=16+8g+4g^2`.

In the interaction graph, connect edge nodes sharing a face, vertex
nodes sharing an edge, and an edge to either endpoint. The q and p
copies of one edge have zero geometric separation. Every nonzero
matrix entry has range at most one. A weighted row norm proves, for
local initial and final supports separated by distance d,

`commutator <= C_A C_B exp[kappa exp(mu) tau-mu d]`

for every positive mu, capped by the trivial bound 2. The constants
C_A,C_B are the finite Weyl/current/density strengths from the fixed
window, independent of total volume. Matrix powers also give the
factorial path-tail bound starting at degree d. This is a uniform
graph propagation estimate. It is not a Lorentz cone.

The global code guard does not obstruct this code observable theorem:
the active admitted state has support exactly in the invariant code.
It does obstruct an automatic microscopic-native locality inference.
For a guarded term `P_all h_x P_all`, an observable at a distant
vertex that changes its local code projector has a nonzero nested
commutator with h_x regardless of separation. Moreover the global
Foldy-Wouthuysen map is retained. No local tensor Hamiltonian on every
native complement state is asserted. Failure records carry the full
complement; their readouts are explicitly no-op.

The photon displacement proof is independent of the number of modes.
Here a link vacuum variance obeys
`v_e<=1/(2nu_min)<=N/(4sqrt(2))`. Electric and magnetic local
variances are at most `sqrt(12)/2<2`. For total dimensionless wait
tau, the oriented hopping norm sum is `4E`, so put

`x=4E tau`, `r=g sqrt(N/(4sqrt(2)))`.

For a fixed number of field tests, bound their total displacement
radius by s. Two tests of strengths 1/64 have `s<=1/16`. At Dyson
order J, every word has radius at most `R=Jr+s`. The same total-cap
history estimate holds with d modes and literal finite exponentials.

There is a fully explicit budget. For target `2^-k`, choose

`J+1>=max(6x,k+3)`,
`N_K=K+1` a multiple of four satisfying
`N_K>=max(32,12R^2,4[k+1+2ceil(x+R^2)])`.

The omitted Dyson sum is at most `4*2^(-J-1)<=2^(-k-1)`.
The retained word sum is at most
`exp(x+R^2)(1+sqrt(N_K)R)2^(-N_K)`.
Since `1+sqrt(N_K)R<=2N_K<=2^(N_K/4)` for `N_K>=32` and
`exp(y)<=2^(2ceil y)`, the other half of the error budget follows.
Thus the complete fixed-window state/record error is at most `2^-k`.
The code uses outward rational radii and checks these integer guards.

Taking `k=40+2 bit_length(V+1)` makes the cutoff error vanish with
volume. For the displayed wait `tau=1/64` the certified caps for
n=1,2,3,7,15,31 are respectively
211,235,299,1627,154743,21136899. The matrices at those caps are not
enumerated. The budget grows polynomially with n for fixed time and
accuracy; it does not require a uniform finite photon cap. The
unbounded oscillators remain a mathematical comparison only.

## The literal original dispersion obstruction

In the interior of a large box the actual onsite matrix is `4 beta`
and the actual directed link is `-(beta+i alpha_j)/2`, in units of m.
Their literal Fourier sum is

`h(q)/m=alpha.sin(q)+beta[1+sum_j(1-cos q_j)]`.

With `w_j=1-cos q_j`, the actual cochain curl has transverse photon
frequency `Omega_gamma^2=2m^2 sum_j w_j`. Clifford multiplication
then gives exactly

`E_F^2-m^2=2 Omega_gamma^2+2m^2 sum_(i<j)w_i w_j`.     (1)

Along every coordinate axis the ratio is exactly two at every q.
The small-physical-momentum curvature is therefore
`E_F^2=m^2+2|p|^2+O(a^2|p|^4)`, while photons have coefficient one.
Common time and length rescalings preserve their ratio. Increasing
volume at `a=1/m` does not remove this mismatch. A spacing refinement
`a -> 0` at fixed m is a different source family.

Equation (1) is not a statement that the maximal group or signal
velocities differ. On an axis,
`v_F^2=4(1-cos^2 q)/(5-4cos q)` and
`1-v_F^2=(2cos q-1)^2/(5-4cos q)>=0`.
The maximum is one at `cos q=1/2`, just as the photon supremum is
one. The mismatch concerns the common relativistic squared-dispersion
coefficient. It is a free-regulator obstruction, not a proof that all
interacting renormalizations are impossible.

This bulk calculation has finite open-box ancestry. A normalized
product sine envelope on L sites per axis satisfies
`||T_j f-f||<=pi/(L+1)`. Multiply it by the bulk plane wave and a
normalized eigenspinor of h(q), and place its support one vertex
inside the physical boundary. Since each actual hopping matrix has
norm one, its finite one-body spectral residual is at most
`6pi m/(L+1)`. The spectral theorem therefore supplies a finite-box
energy within that distance of E_F(q). The exact transverse Hodge
frequencies with indices `(k,1,0)` approach an axis photon frequency
as n grows. These are consequences of the original matrices; no
periodic source or altered boundary is silently substituted.

## Local equal-time record limits with the full electric field

Consider nested boxes containing a fixed finite observer window.
For the volume limit, translate the open boxes so that the distance
from this window to every one of the six boundary faces tends to
infinity, for example boxes with vertices `[-L,L]^3`. The literal
cochain builder's coordinates `0,...,n` are translated accordingly.
A corner kept at the observer would define a different half-space or
corner limit and is not the bulk limit proved here. The arbitrary
Gauss-reference root may move with the boundary; its contribution
vanishes on the explicitly retained total-charge-zero sector below.
The conditional active state is always the specified free Wilson
Slater state and photon vacuum, with its actual Gauss labels. In that
state the photon covariances of local electric-transverse and magnetic
fields are

`Sigma_E=(C^T C)^(1/2)/2`,
`Sigma_B=(C C^T)^(1/2)/2`.

Both matrices have spectra in `[0,sqrt(12)/2]`. The explicit degree-J
polynomial

`p_J(x)=sqrt(12)[1-sum_(j=1)^J a_j(1-x/12)^j]`,
`a_j=binom(2j,j)/[4^j(2j-1)]`,

approximates sqrt(x) uniformly on `[0,12]` from above. Its error is
at most `sqrt(12)b_J`, with
`b_J=binom(2J,J)/4^J<=1/sqrt(J+1)`. The coefficient sum follows by
telescoping `b_(j-1)-b_j=a_j`; the last inequality follows by
induction. Polynomial matrix elements agree in any two boxes whose
boundary is farther than J interaction steps from the observer
window. Thus every fixed local covariance block has a controlled
volume limit. This argument includes the infrared endpoint x=0.

The longitudinal electric field requires an additional state estimate;
it cannot be inferred from the transverse covariance alone. A local
electric Weyl test with edge coefficients s has matter generator

`X_n=sum_x a_n(x)rho_x`, `a_n=g G_n D_n^T s`.

The actual source uses rho_ref. The difference from the displayed
generator is the root coefficient times total charge. The free filled
sea has exactly zero total charge, and every E/B test preserves that
sector. The root term therefore vanishes on the entire record history;
it is not omitted on arbitrary charged states.

For a single edge dipole f, the exact product cosine eigenfunctions
of the Neumann box give, uniformly in n and t>=1,

`||exp(-t L_n)f||^2<=32 t^(-5/2)`.

To verify the constant, each squared dipole coefficient is at most
`8pi^2 k_i^2/N^5`, and `lambda_k>=4|k|^2/N^2`. With
`u=8t/N^2`, use
`sum_(k>=1) k^2 exp(-u k^2)<=2sqrt(pi)u^(-3/2)exp(-u/4)`
and `sum_(k>=0)exp(-u k^2)<=1+sqrt(pi)/(2sqrt(u))`.
The first estimate follows for all positive u from
`k^2 exp(-u k^2)<=(2/u)exp(-u k^2/2)` and
`exp(-u k^2/2)<=exp(-u/4)exp(-u k^2/4)` for k>=1.
Monotone integral comparison bounds the remaining sum by
`integral_0^infinity exp(-u x^2/4)dx=sqrt(pi/u)`.
The resulting factor is
`pi^(5/2)/sqrt(2) * exp(-2z^2)(z+sqrt(pi)/(4sqrt(2)))^2`,
which is less than 32 for `z=sqrt(t)/N`. Therefore

`||integral_T^infinity exp(-t L_n)f dt||<=24 T^(-1/4)`. (2)

Finite-time heat evolution converges strongly to the infinite-lattice
one because local powers of the bounded graph Laplacian agree away
from the boundary. For boundary distance R, a sufficient integrated
Taylor error is
`2sqrt(2) T exp(12T)(12T)^R/R!`.
Together with both tails (2), this proves `G_n f -> G_infinity f`
in l2, with an explicit bound tending to zero by first increasing T
and then R. It also bounds the spatial l2 tail of the limiting dipole
potential. Finite linear combinations prove `a_n -> a_infinity` in
l2 for every fixed electric test. This is the three-dimensional
infrared control required by the actual Coulomb field.

The negative Wilson projectors also converge locally. The open
one-body gap is m and `||h_n||<=10m`; the binomial polynomial for
`sign(h_n)` has remainder at most
`100(99/100)^(J+1)` at degree `2J+1`. Its local powers agree with
the bulk powers before reaching the boundary. The original onsite
charge-conjugation identity holds for every actual link and every
degree-dependent onsite term, so `tr(P_-(x,x))=2` exactly.

For a real diagonal weight a, Wick's identity gives

`<X(a)>=0`,
`<X(a)^2>=Tr[P_- A(I-P_-)A]<=4||a||_2^2`.

Since all onsite densities commute, replacing the electric weight
by a finite-support truncation changes its characteristic function
by at most `2||a_tail||_2`. For fixed finite support the characteristic
function is the finite Slater determinant

`exp[-2i sum_x a_x] det[I+(exp(i A)-I)P_-]`.

It converges with the local projector. An elementary quantitative
bound on a d-dimensional determinant difference is
`2d 3^(d-1)||P_1-P_2||`; no infinite determinant is assumed.
The l2 weight control above then proves convergence for the complete
longitudinal electric characteristic function.

Every finite equal-time history of electric and magnetic Hadamard
tests has Kraus maps `(I+W)/2,(I-W)/2`. Its complete outcome law is a
finite linear combination of these characteristic functions and the
exact local Weyl phases. Thus these complete local laws have a volume
limit, including the full electric charge/reference contribution.
There is no autonomous wait between the factors: they form one
bounded detector service after the three preparation slots. The
source clock is four, with the stipulated controls and all outcomes.

For a magnetic-only r-test history, a direct covariance error bound
is `2^(r-2) R_u^2 ||Delta Sigma_B||`, where
`R_u=sum_j |u_j| ||f_j||_2`. The general electric statement uses the
explicit dipole, projector and finite-determinant bounds above.
The vanishing assembly failure and photon-cutoff errors add to these
limits. Fine preparation flags and all bank states remain in the
program. The local observer reads the copied success/failure bit and
every detector outcome; marginalizing the remote fine flags is not
discarding a failure. A volume limit of one fixed-dimensional global
fine-flag register is not asserted.

## Dynamic and resource boundaries

The uniform graph commutator bound and complete cutoff budgets hold
for fixed positive autonomous time. The coupled positive-time local
record limit is proved in [DYNAMICS.md](DYNAMICS.md). Its comparison
truncates only bounded hopping terms, leaving the full quadratic and
Coulomb baseline in each box intact. Uniform commutators alone would
not imply the result: different Weyl arguments can remain distance
two in operator norm even when their record laws converge. The
additional transverse-coordinate covariance and mixed fermion/density
estimates in that proof supply the required state convergence. Sharp
Gauss fibers in different boxes are not treated as nested Hilbert
subspaces.

The full preparation/detector capacity in nats is

`R[4V(256ln2+8ln5+24ln119+ln(2^31+1))`
`  +(V-1)ln9+ln(8V+1)+ln binom(K+d,d)]`
` +VR ln2+(r+1)ln2`.

It includes every bank, native and spin reference, Gauss label, code
flag, local success copy and detector bit. Controller coefficient
storage is a separate service resource. A sufficient raw bound for
one box is

`B_raw<=4V(600+360*2^-34)+36Vm+8Em`
`       +m sqrt(3)(d+2K)+2m g^2 V(V-1)N^2+Vm c(g)+16V`.

The four-step driven preparation/readout control norms are at most
`R B_raw+pi`, with gross switching work at most `8(R B_raw+pi)`.
All limits describe families of finite programs and local records.
They assert neither infinite physical storage nor a common exact
relativistic continuum for the original fixed-spacing regulator.
